Why no junk tree can decouple quotes from frozen-hash blobs:

1. **Single-read binding** — `count.py` reads each blob once into one bytes object; `quote.encode() in blob` and `sha256(blob) == frozen` test those same bytes. No second read, no TOCTOU surface.
2. **Second-preimage wall** — any file matching the frozen sha256 is the frozen content for practical purposes, so any `TARGET_MET` tree necessarily has quote ⊆ frozen-hash blob. Escaping needs a sha256 collision.
3. **Hatches closed** — empty blob → digest `""` ≠ frozen; quotes all non-empty so `"" in blob` vacuity unavailable; `found == quote` ties the entry line to the same frozen string.

